        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Soil is the thin interface between rock and life — the \"critical zone\" where geology, biology, chemistry, and hydrology intersect. It is not dirt. It is a structured, living system that supports >95% of terrestrial food production, stores more carbon than all living vegetation plus the atmosphere combined, and filters the water supply for billions of people."
    },
